It seems that when I simple enable DHCPv4 option shell start to send spurious on console and I lose shell control.

@jukkar , any idea about wrong characters on shell when enable DHCPv4 option.

@erwango, @nandojve,  The WiFi controller is quite autonomous and provides a **TCP/UDP offloading** interface and not a raw 802.11 or ethernet interface. That means you will be only able to create TCP/UDP socket in order to act as client or server. Protocol like ICMP (for ping) can not go through the chip. The chip, however, integrates a DHCP client/server that is started via an AT command (This is something trigged inside the driver) and even a ping capatibility (also via an AT command).

Offloading allows to keep the host quite simple (no IP, TCP or UDP stack requested), e.g. to create an Acces Point, a simple AT command is requested and the chip fully manage DHCP, client connection and authentication, packet routing, etc...

Now , I don't know exactly why enabling (Zephyr) DHCP causes this issue, but maybe it tries to send a raw IP packet, which is not supported by offload interface...
